h  um but the council's duty of course is  to all of the districts  residents and that's why we took the  program approach  to ensure that all six sites would be  regenerated rather than just singling  out one or two  um and it's worth pointing out i think  that as part of our  outline business case analysis we did  consider  the merits of consolidating all council  activity at the mill site  but our analysis showed that that wasn't  the best value for money  so i think that's probably as much as i  can contribute at this stage mike  lovely thanks angela i'm afraid to say  that not for the first time i've ever  run  my time and i'm afraid that time has  beaten us and i want to start to bring  the meeting to a conclusion please i do  hope that everybody has found it very  interesting  and informative but also it's gone a  long way to answer some of the questions  the queries and the things you didn't  really understand i would like please to  say just a few words  of thanks to all the panelists who've  been working behind the scenes  to paul wilkins and colleagues from  missouri to nikki to dawn and others at  both  rochester district council and gb  partnerships in the background  who've done very much wonderful work in  helping all the arrangements for this  evening's  presentation would just mention that  although we're going to close the  presentation the moment  the webinar will remain open for up to  10 minutes  just in case you've got any further  questions you want to ask but please  remember that the consultation period is  still  ongoing and you still have chances if  you reflect in a day or two  on any other questions that you forgot  to ask or didn't realize or on  reflection  everybody within this project is very  very keen to have you  give you give them your views but i'd  now please like to pass and return to  councillor simon wooten  to say a final few words this evening  councillor wooden  thank you chairman uh a personal thank  you to you for the  